Hi Mike,

I can't seem to get a simulated ectotherm to experience any desiccation. I looked up related conversations in the Google Group, and found this one between you and Adam in 2021 <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CVlWGOGKSnVwGzCJyAGP_090/https%3A%2F%2Fgroups.google.com%2Fg%2Fnichemapr%2Fc%2F2KuIIBcZgOE%2Fm%2FBsAgTNREAgAJ%3Futm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter>. Following the steps you suggested there, and doing some other tweaking to simulate what I believe should be an animal that's pretty terrible at holding water, I still see no desiccation (as indicated by PCT_DESIC). Below I provide a toy example, run using the most recent build on GitHub as of today. Can you point me towards how I can get this toy animal to start desiccating?

Thanks,
Dave
library(NicheMapR)
library(ggplot2)

micro <- micro_global(loc = c(145.620, -16.821), PCTWET = 50) #Kuranda, Queensland

ecto <- ectotherm(T_F_min = 30, T_F_max = 35, T_pref = 33, T_B_min = 20,
                  T_RB_min = 10,
                  DEB = 1, # Turn DEB model on
                  fossorial = 0, aestdepth = 1, # prevent belowground activity
                  pct_H_P = 99, pct_H_N = 99, pct_wet = 100, # maximize water loss
                  pct_H_X = .1,  # minimize water gain
                  raindrink = 1000, # Very high threshold necessary for drinking (mm of rainfall)
                  K_skin = 10, psi_body = -707, H2Obal_init = -1)

# Extract predictions
debout = as.data.frame(ecto$debout)
yearsout = as.data.frame(ecto$yearsout)
yearout = as.data.frame(ecto$yearout)

debout$timestep <- 1:nrow(debout)

# No change to percent desiccation
ggplot(debout) +
  geom_point(aes(timestep, PCT_DESIC))

# No reported desiccation in summary matrices
yearsout$MaxDes
yearout$Pct_Des

--
David Klinges, PhD

