Hello Michael,

Thank you for your detailed advice! I am interested in high rainforest, so I might need to try microclimc (micropoint).
But after adjusting specific parameter (leaf area index, roughness height, water in air, wind speed), microclimate still works well and close to actual air temperature at near-surface height for rainforest. Maybe others can refer it.

'''
  micro <- micro_era5(
                      loc=coor,
                      dstart=dstart, dfinish=dfinish,
                      Usrhyt=1.1,
                      Refhyt=2,
                      CMH2O=2,
                      rainwet=1.5,
                      microclima.LAI=5,
                      minshade=0,maxshade=100,
                      coastal=T, cad.effects=T,
                      RUF=0.02, # rainforest
                      windfac=0.1,
                      soilgrids=0
  )
'''
